I found 9 issues in `fix-declared-caps-builtins` at f81d54109. None is a crash. The most serious ones are ways the new capability guard can miss a direct type assertion that it is supposed to catch.

The guard and the architecture tests pass locally; the guard takes 0.23s over 737 production Go files. The detection gaps in findings 1 and 2 come from reading the code. I did not prove them with a planted file, because that would have meant adding a file to the worktree.

